w that said on holds a  mysterious weapon most players didn't  take a close look at his hip and  suspected that this was just a silver  sword but it's actually a completely  unique blade that's not listed anywhere  it's an extremely rare occurrence but  some lozalfos when carrying two handed  weapons can put up their arm to block  attacks barehanded this can be guard  broken as well  [Music]  on the main menu screen and in all the  game art for breath of the wild there  are some beautiful shots of link looking  upon the wide land of hyrule while the  ground link is standing or climbing on  is prettied up for promotional purposes  the views he's looking at are real  locations in the game such as this one  climbing the tall cliff looking north  east next to mount grenade and this one  facing northeast right on top of satori  mountain  [Music]  and this one facing northwest from the  top of the dueling peaks  there's an interesting side effect found  through the memory storage glitch that  allows you to save a save file but  without actually having the game started  if this happens the save file will be  blank but say it was saved on january  1st of 1970. this date is actually less  about breath of the wild itself and is  more about how time is recorded  internationally called unix time it's a  system that sets the date based on the  number of values given to it if the  number is zero from this glitch it sets  it to what's called the unix epoch the  beginning of the system started on  january 1st of 1970. there are a few  select places in the game that require  you to shoot down ropes to drop the ramp  for you well on the chances that you get  the angle to just line them both up and  shoot both ropes at the same time  or you know just throw a well-placed  boomerang instead  did you know that the zora used goron  tools  if you look closely at the stone smiths  repairing the zora domain they're all  using a hammer and chisel and these have  the the dongo footprint goron 